      "writtenOn": "2025-05-28T04:03:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "this should be passed as an owning ref to avoid the possibility of a dangling pointer. Since you can\u0027t easily pass a `Ref\u003cDevice\u003e`, I think you can use `APIAddRef`/`APIRelease` directly.\n\nThough ideally (if possible) we could use the C++ `wgpu::DeviceDescriptor` and `wgpu::DeviceDescriptor::SetDeviceLostCallback`, which can handle capturing lambdas, and just capture a `Ref\u003cDevice\u003e`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 102,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 102,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "67082840b5999585368eadf7034efbbc8e0e60b6",
